# Copy to a .txt file (or pass any file to `python -m euresis learn <file>`).
# formula   | domain | name | equation | symbol:quantity_id ...
# principle | domain | name | statement
# quantity  | id | name | SI dimension (e.g. M L2 T-2)
# constant  | symbol | name | value | unit | SI dimension
# frontier  | domain | open problem | q:quantity c:constant ...
